WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:05.470
Few comic book characters conjure up horror
and then heroism, and then back to horror

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:06.440
again, better than Venom.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:11.920
Since debuting in Amazing Spider-Man #300,
it wrapped its tendrils into the hearts of

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.100
fans everywhere.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.990
With a new film starring Tom Hardy on the
way, you may think you know all there is to

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.160
know about the symbiote.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:23.480
But Venom has a long and curious history at
Marvel that goes deeper than most people realize.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:24.880
Fan-made

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:29.660
The idea for Venom began life as nothing more
than a costume change for Peter Parker, when

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:34.700
Spider-fan Randy Schueller submitted what
he called a "stealth suit" for a Marvel competition.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:40.820
Marvel Editor-in-Chief Jim Shooter bought
the costume idea for $220, and gave Schueller

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.100
a chance to write the story.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:47.300
John Byrne and Roger Stern later altered the
original concept and made it into a self-repairing

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:52.579
costume for Spidey before David Michelinie
and Todd McFarlane gave Venom his signature

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.000
look and characteristics.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:59.480
Ironically, Schueller wasn't a fan of his
design's villainous turn, saying he was "disturbed"

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:00.840
by the costume-gone-wild.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.820
It wasn't until he saw Venom on the big screen
in Spider-Man 3 that he finally came to terms

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:06.320
with it.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.660
Grandpa Venom

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:14.430
In Amazing Spider-Man #333, Venom goes toe-to-toe
with the villainous Styx and comes out on

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:15.780
the losing end of the battle.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:21.180
Venom disintegrates, Eddie Brock goes to jail,
and for awhile it seemed like the symbiote

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.440
had met its maker for good.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.200
But, of course, he comes back.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:30.280
Venom returned to break Eddie Brock out of
prison in Amazing Spider-Man #345, and he

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:35.659
left something behind: a homicidal bundle
of joy named Carnage, who bonded with convicted

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:40.160
serial killer Cletus Kasady in Amazing Spider-Man
#361.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.780
"Kasady is gone!

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:44.840
There is only Carnage!"

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:50.200
Roughly a decade later, Carnage made Venom
a grandaddy-symbiote, bearing and then trying

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.060
to kill its own rugrat, Toxin, in Venom Vs.
Carnage.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:58.859
After Toxin's first host was killed, it found
yet another kindred spirit in who else but

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.740
longtime host Eddie Brock, who got the pleasure
of hosting two generations of symbiote.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.660
Video game upload

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:11.380
Marvel got super-meta in 1995 when it released
Venom: Carnage Unleashed, a comic about a

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:15.740
game that's based on a real-life video game
called Maximum Carnage.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:20.560
The four-issue story finds Carnage using the
game's server to upload himself into phone

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.080
lines.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.380
Because, you know, internet in the '90s.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:32.700
Naturally, Venom joins the hunt for the cybernetic
symbiote and eventually wins the day.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:37.320
Considering dial-up speeds at the time, the
biggest twist is that Carnage managed to upload

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.860
so much as a finger before the story ended.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:41.420
Venom for sale

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.340
For Venom fans, there's really only one true
host: Eddie Brock.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:50.560
But before becoming Venom's host, Brock was
dying of cancer, and when Eddie's cancer returned,

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.240
he chose to make a few changes to his vigilante
lifestyle.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.730
Brock decided the best way to be rid of Venom
was auctioning it off for charity in Marvel

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:02.570
Knights Spider-Man #6—nothing could go wrong
with that plan, right?

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:07.040
The suit ends up with Angelo, the son of a
local mob boss, who proceeds to slaughter

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.240
several of Peter Parker's classmates.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.420
Great decision, Eddie.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:12.520
Identity crisis

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:16.980
Most of us assume that Venom and its host
act as one organism when they're merged, but

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.480
Venom does have its own voice, and it doesn't
always agree with its host.

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:26.940
While Venom and Eddie Brock usually got along,
2016's Venom reboot had Venom finding a new

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.440
host in former Army Ranger Lee Price.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.860
And they bickered like an old married couple.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:37.220
Venom continuously criticized Price's behavior
and callous violence—even trying to sabotage

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.740
his criminal activities.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.380
Of course, once Spider-Man teases it with
a reunion, Venom reverts to its rage-filled

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:43.900
state.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.480
Way to crush all that character development,
Spidey.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:47.540
Very uncool.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:48.840
Lady Venom

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:54.080
According to the book Comics Creators on Spider-Man,
Venom was originally conceived as a female

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:54.600
villain.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.220
As Spidey writer David Michelinie explained,
the idea was for a woman to go into labor

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:03.300
after her husband was accidentally killed
during one of Spider-Man's battles.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:08.520
Her child tragically dies during birth, and
she's consumed by misdirected hatred toward

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:09.080
the Web-head.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:13.780
The symbiote seeks her out, and the two bond
over their loathing and hunt down Spider-Man.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:18.380
Obviously, the idea never made it into the
comics, but hey, there's always a chance it'll

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.340
come back in a future Venom reboot.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.480
Deadpool wrecked Venom's mind

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:27.520
Comic book companies love - to mess with continuity,
and that goes double for the writers of Deadpool.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:32.500
In Deadpool's Secret Secret Wars, the story
goes that Wade Wilson first discovered the

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.320
alien symbiote.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:38.349
Not only does the revamp revel in lampooning
the epic crossover, one of Marvel's first

00:04:38.349 --> 00:04:43.110
major events, but it also gives Deadpool a
chance to rewrite history in his inimitable

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:43.620
fashion.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.980
But Wade quickly recognizes that the suit
is sentient, and he doesn't think it's fair

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.420
to any living creature to make it spend time
in his screwed up head.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:56.360
So he rejects the symbiote, worrying that
he's "driven it nuts or something," just before

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.340
Spider-Man gets to it.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:00.200
Basically, Deadpool created the Venom we all
know.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.820
Natural predator

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.700
When you're a symbiotic life form, life is
pretty sweet.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:07.880
For the most part, Venom really doesn't have
much to fear.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.120
However, the symbiotes do have one known predator.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:16.740
In the 1996 miniseries, Venom: The Hunted,
our friendly neighborhood conjoined antihero

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:21.860
was stalked by a Xenophage, an alien species
with a taste for symbiote-host brainwaves.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:26.720
Xenophages are particularly dangerous because
they transmute themselves into other shapes.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.940
At one point it even hid out as a china cabinet,
of all things.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:31.980
Species origin

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:37.380
Although Venom received a semi-backstory in
the "Planet of the Symbiotes" arc in 1995,

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:42.599
which revealed an entire planet of the parasitic
life forms, the alien race didn't get an official

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.300
name for another 20 years.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:49.020
During his time kicking it with Flash Thompson
and the Guardians of the Galaxy, Venom finally

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:51.180
received an official origin story.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:57.000
Guardians #23 introduced the Klyntar species
and explained that the symbiotes are usually

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.180
pretty nice guys.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.960
They just need to bond with evenly balanced
hosts.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:05.960
When their hosts have a couple screws loose,
a symbiote easily becomes corrupted—which

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:08.300
is what happened with Venom and Eddie Brock.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.260
It also didn't hurt that Venom spent some
time inside Deadpool's head.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.420
"Ohhhhh, that's not good."

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:16.160
Thanks for watching!

